<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <style name="Theme.MCCConstruction" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />

    <!--
        The launch theme, and the app's actual brand moment.

        Android 12+ always draws a system splash over a cold start and holds it
        until the app renders its first frame. A Compose "splash screen" behind
        that is invisible: ours lived 1400ms, which expired underneath the system
        splash, so the branded screen was never seen on API 31+ and users went
        straight from the system splash to Login. Rather than fight it, the
        system splash IS the branding now.

        Kept light in both light and dark mode on purpose. The mark is fixed
        navy-and-gold artwork on transparency, so it needs a light ground, and a
        white splash also hands over cleanly to the white Login surface with no
        flash between them.

        The icon is the launcher foreground, so the icon the user tapped is the
        one that grows into the splash.

        Deliberately no setKeepOnScreenCondition: the splash lasts exactly as
        long as startup does. Holding it longer would re-add the artificial delay
        this replaces.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.MCCConstruction.Splash" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/brand_splash_background</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/Theme.MCCConstruction</item>
    </style>
</resources>
